  "★ True End": "★ 真结局",
  "Plain Love": "平凡的爱",
  "A few years after the A-levels. Hanis is deep into her nursing degree. You're deep into {passion}, your course and your own plans. Neither of you shrank to fit the other.\nYou still meet at the dragon playground at Seri Bayu. You still argue sometimes, and fix it before it sets. You know her real favourites now, not the ones you guessed.\nOn your desk: a photo of a nasi lemak with the egg cut into a heart. On her phone: a budget you made together. It balances.\nMochi, from the windowsill: \"Not fireworks. A fire you both keep lit. The good kind.\"": "A水准考完几年后。哈妮丝在她的护理学位里忙得不得了。你忙着{passion}、你的课和你自己的计划。你们谁都没有为了迁就对方把自己缩小。\n你们还是会在斯里巴尤的龙形游乐场见面。有时还是会吵，但会在变成心结之前讲开。你现在知道她真正喜欢什么，不是你以前猜的那些。\n你的桌上：一张照片：一份椰浆饭，鸡蛋切成了心形。她的手机里：一份你们一起做的预算。收支平衡。\n麻糬在窗台上说：“不是烟火。是一把你们一起顾着的火。好的那种。”",
  "Normal End": "普通结局",
  "Still Learning": "还在学",
  "Hanis and you are still together. Most days are good. Some days one of you goes quiet instead of saying the hard thing, or the calendar only has room for one of your lives.\nNone of it is a disaster. It's all habit, and habits can change.\nMochi: \"You passed, rookie. Not with honours. Keep practising the boring parts. Those ARE the romantic parts.\"": "你和哈妮丝还在一起。大部分日子都不错。有些日子，你们其中一个选择不讲话，而不是讲那句难开口的话；或者日程表只排得下其中一个人的生活。\n这些都不是灾难。都是习惯，而习惯是可以改的。\n麻糬：“你及格了，菜鸟。不是优等。继续练那些无聊的部分。那些才是真正浪漫的部分。”",
  "Good End": "好结局",
  "A Kind Goodbye": "好好地说再见",
  "You and Hanis ended it in the year that tested everyone. Nobody shouted. Nobody posted anything. You said thank you, and meant it.\nA year later she sends a photo from her nursing degree. You send one back from your own first real step with {passion}. You're both, quietly, better people than the two kids who met in JC1.\nMochi: \"Ending well is still love. You lost a girlfriend, not yourself.\"": "在那个考验每个人的一年，你和哈妮丝分开了。没有人大吵。没有人发帖。你说了谢谢，而且是真心的。\n一年后，她传来一张她的护理学位的照片。你回传一张你在{passion}上踏出第一步的照片。你们两个都悄悄地，比当年初院一年级认识的那两个小孩更好了。\n麻糬：“好好结束，也是爱。你失去的是女朋友，不是你自己。”",
  "A few years after the A-levels. Xin Yi is deep into her writing programme in Melbourne. You're deep into {passion}, your course and your own plans. Neither of you shrank to fit the other.\nYou still meet at the bookshop on the third floor of the mall. You still argue sometimes, and fix it before it sets. You know her real favourites now, not the ones you guessed.\nOn your desk: a manuscript with your name in the acknowledgements, spelled right this time. On her phone: a budget you made together. It balances.\nMochi, from the windowsill: \"Not fireworks. A fire you both keep lit. The good kind.\"": "A水准考完几年后。欣怡在她在墨尔本的写作课程里忙得不得了。你忙着{passion}、你的课和你自己的计划。你们谁都没有为了迁就对方把自己缩小。\n你们还是会在商场三楼那间书店见面。有时还是会吵，但会在变成心结之前讲开。你现在知道她真正喜欢什么，不是你以前猜的那些。\n你的桌上：一份书稿，致谢里有你的名字，这次拼对了。她的手机里：一份你们一起做的预算。收支平衡。\n麻糬在窗台上说：“不是烟火。是一把你们一起顾着的火。好的那种。”",
