  "A few years after the A-levels. Kavya is deep into her athletics scholarship. You're deep into {passion}, your course and your own plans. Neither of you shrank to fit the other.\nYou still meet at the track at dawn. You still argue sometimes, and fix it before it sets. You know her real favourites now, not the ones you guessed.\nOn your desk: a race bib from her first college meet, mailed with a sticky note: \"you waited, I ran\". On her phone: a budget you made together. It balances.\nMochi, from the windowsill: \"Not fireworks. A fire you both keep lit. The good kind.\"": "A水准考完几年后。卡维娅在她的田径奖学金里忙得不得了。你忙着{passion}、你的课和你自己的计划。你们谁都没有为了迁就对方把自己缩小。\n你们还是会在清晨的跑道见面。有时还是会吵，但会在变成心结之前讲开。你现在知道她真正喜欢什么，不是你以前猜的那些。\n你的桌上：她大学第一场比赛的号码布，寄来时贴着一张便利贴：“你等了，我跑了”。她的手机里：一份你们一起做的预算。收支平衡。\n麻糬在窗台上说：“不是烟火。是一把你们一起顾着的火。好的那种。”",
